# Private strings that must never reach a published file, one extended-regex per
# line. Blank lines and lines beginning with # are ignored; matching is
# case-insensitive. `hq-publish-check` scans the publishable file set against
# these before you make the repo public.
#
# These are YOUR values, so this file ships only as an example. Copy it to
# `.publish-denylist` (gitignored) and replace the lines below with your own:
# every email you use, any cloud/account IDs, and the names of private or client
# projects that must not appear in public docs, comments, or examples.
#
# Do NOT list your own name here — attribution in LICENSE and README is expected
# and would only produce false positives.
#
# Escape a literal dot as [.] so it does not match any character:
#
#   you@example[.]com
#   you@work[.]edu
#   0000-0000-0000
#   private-client-name
#   secret-project-slug
